# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Warm-up seed list  —  consenting recipients ONLY
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Copy this file to  warmup_seeds.txt  (same folder) and fill it in.
#   cp clients/<client>/warmup_seeds.txt.template clients/<client>/warmup_seeds.txt
#
# scripts/warmup_send.py sends a few small, personal warm-up emails per day to
# the addresses listed here, so those people can REPLY / mark "not spam" and
# teach the mail providers that this domain is legitimate.
#
# RULES
#   • One email address per line.
#   • Only addresses you control, or people who have AGREED to receive these.
#     These are NOT prospects. Never put a stranger here.
#   • '#' starts a comment; blank lines are ignored.
#   • Both  name@example.com  and  Name <name@example.com>  work.
#   • The real warmup_seeds.txt is gitignored — it never gets committed.
#
# TIP: spread across providers (Gmail, Outlook, Yahoo) for a stronger signal,
# and pick people who will actually reply — a reply is the #1 reputation signal.
#
# Examples (delete these, add your own):
# you@gmail.com
# your.other@outlook.com
# a.friend@yahoo.com
